From 3b0959dc8dd2bc86db95a06238c4a79962b1665e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex Executor <codex-executor@local>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 03:12:28 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 04/22] Sheet label production command, unit tests, and a
 carrier-map defect fix

- produce_sheet_label.py: create-only label directory, resolution presets (fast/production/reference), carrier 1/32,
  fail-closed on empty cells (status EMPTY, no operator), on port support escaping the geometric active set, on a rigid
  residual above 1e-10 and on a negative eigenvalue; writes the operator on the active set together with carrier ids,
  coordinates, port membership, rigid basis, and the carrier mass and Laplace-Beltrami matrices the training loss needs,
  plus SHA-256 receipts recording the git head, resolution and execution settings.
- Reproducibility: geometry is byte-identical across repeats and thread counts; the operator is byte-identical at a
  fixed thread count and agrees to 2e-14 across thread counts (MKL summation order), so the receipt pins the threads.
- test_sheet_solid_surface.py (5 tests) covers the level set, plane clipping with shared cut vertices, the constrained
  Newton projection, watertightness plus the published density law, and the geometric active carrier set. It caught a
  defect: the carrier-node to surface-vertex map was built before fragment removal and vertex merging renumbered the
  vertices, so the mesher preservation check tested the wrong vertices. The map is now rebuilt by coordinate and is the
  cap conformity certificate (G0: 1086 carrier nodes on the surface, all preserved exactly by Gmsh). Labels were not
  affected: the port map is compiled geometrically from the mesh.

